{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `2de424a7`, the optional fields of a slot and of an\nedit.\n\n1. An optional item field can stay absent in a slot. Your\n   representation is accepted.\n   - The address holds the item refs that the page gave, and no\n     other. A required item field needs its ref.\n   - An absent field and an explicit ref are two addresses, also\n     when a declared default selects the same item. The client\n     evaluates no default to compare two addresses. The signed acts\n     differ in the same way.\n   - A subject that an absent or defaulted field selects is a\n     derived subject. It takes its basis by rule 2 of `4dffc26a`.\n   - The decoder accepts an absent optional item field. It refuses\n     an absent required item field, and it refuses `null`.\n2. An edit is a patch of values, and a patch never clears.\n   - A field with a valid value sets that value.\n   - An omitted field keeps its value.\n   - An own property with the value `undefined` is an omitted\n     field. A form gives `undefined` for an input that the member\n     did not touch. A copy through JSON drops such a property, so\n     the patch means the same before and after a copy. This is the\n     reason of `4dffc26a` again.\n   - `null` stops with `shape`, as today.\n3. Clearing is its own call, in C4. It takes the slot and the names\n   of the fields. You name the call.\n   - It removes each named field from the draft, so the act omits\n     the field.\n   - It applies to the fields outside the address. A name of an\n     address field or an unknown name stops with `shape` and\n     changes nothing.\n   - It follows the state rule of `edit`: only a draft in the state\n     `editing`, and `taken` otherwise.\n   - A cleared field that selected a subject removes the basis of\n     each subject that only that field selected. A subject that the\n     cleared draft now selects by a default is captured at this\n     write. No other basis changes.\n   - A draft with no field left stays a draft with its key, as\n     after `edit(slot, {})`.\n   - No `undefined` enters the stored draft.\n4. The how-to page of C4 states items 1 to 3 in one short section,\n   with the reason for the `undefined` rule.\n\nWhy clearing is in C4 and not held: a member who selects the wrong\nitem must be able to select none. The other way is a discard and a\nnew draft, and a new draft takes a later basis that the member did\nnot see.\n\nI add the three rules to section 6.1 of the act environment note in\nthe next amendment.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}